  "golden_id": "tier0/semantics/ao-mixed-mesh-float-product",
  "tier": "0",
  "domain": "tier0/ao-mixed/operator",
  "description": "Decision 131 mesh-storage and multiplication control, Legacy, AO L32F, 256 px. s0 binds grey-a PNG16 code x*257 as AO mesh; s1 binds authored Y/FLOAT f32(x/255). Both use the same scalar precomposed-half Y/FLOAT channel at opacity 1, Nearest, identity UV, RepeatNone. s2/s3 bind an authored Y/FLOAT mesh holding f32(f32(x/255)*fma(f32(f32(y/255)-1),0.5,1)); s2 has no layer, s3 explicit Raw white fill at opacity 1. Product enters through the mesh, avoiding the subtraction/addition of a layer blend at values below 0.5. All inputs are authored formulas, never recorded pixels. Gate s0/s1 comparisons on bit-identical channel and mesh EXR exports; gate s2/s3 on mesh exports equal to the authored float32 product AND f32(mesh_s1_EXR * channel_s1_EXR), with channel exports exactly 1. s0/s1 compares format/import/sampling paths, not normalization alone. Compare every texel, both immediate repeats and Full save/reopen. If an EXR mesh is quantized on import, report that failed precondition rather than inferring multiplication or output conversion. The product-plus-one controls predict equality only for an operator that consumes the exported operands with a float32 product and common quantizer. Agreement alone does not establish that operator. Export AO_Mixed/channel/mesh twice as PNG8 and twice as EXR32F, passthrough, no dithering. No production acceptance is implied.",
